window.docContents[108].resolve({"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--A-New--add--Rule":{"contents":"Here is another fundamental rule about addition:n + (succ m) = succ (n + m).This is the rule we need to push succ around.Here it is in Lean:\n\n\n\ntheorem add_succ : ∀ n m : Nat, n + (succ m) = succ (n + m) := by\n  intro n m\n  rfl\n\n\nNow, let's use add_succ in a proof:\n\ntheorem add_one (n : Nat) : n + (succ zero) = succ n + zero := by\n  rewrite [add_succ]\n  rewrite [add_zero]\n  rewrite [add_zero]\n  rfl\n\n\nWe recommend stepping through these proofs in VS Code —\nthat is, moving past each tactic with your cursor to see how it\nchanges the proof state and hovering over each argument to rewrite to see its type.\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Proof by Rewriting","header":"2.2.5. A New  add  Rule","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--A-New--add--Rule"}});